From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:22:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/50] nxhost nvn: write CPU-readable linear render targets
 back to guest memory

A game that renders into a linear texture (LINEAR or LINEAR_RENDER_TARGET)
in a CPU-readable pool reads the result from that memory after a fence
wait; the host drew into a separate Metal texture and never copied it
back, so the CPU kept seeing stale bytes. Splatoon 3 hands GPU results to
its game code this way (1x1, 2x2 and 128x1 RGBA32F targets). When a pass
ends, such color targets are now blitted into guest memory at their row
pitch, in the same command buffer, so the copy is complete when the
game's fence wait returns. NX_CPU_TARGET_WRITEBACK=0 turns it off;
NX_TRACE_CPU_TARGETS=1 logs the first writebacks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013yetZ2nJDh2A6QWpF2QWuu
